From: Stained Glass OS <ke7oxh@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] win32u: a host font's entry in the Fonts key comes back when it was taken away

win32u writes each host font (fontconfig's) into HKLM\...\Fonts and remembers that it did in
HKCU\Software\Wine\Fonts\External Fonts. On the next start, a font it remembered was taken as
still listed. An installer that ships the same font deletes the entry when it is uninstalled:
LibreOffice's MSI removes "Liberation Sans (TrueType)". The entry then stayed gone for good, and
so did 7711's arial.ttf link to Liberation Sans. Java programs (Scilab 2027 on qa5) then drew
every letter as a box. Now a remembered font whose entry is missing is written again. An entry
that an installer changed to point at its own file is left alone.

--- a/dlls/win32u/font.c
+++ b/dlls/win32u/font.c
@@ -6933,6 +6933,25 @@
         if ((tmp = wcsrchr( value, ' ' )) && !facename_compare( tmp, true_type_suffixW, -1 )) *tmp = 0;
         if ((face = find_face_from_full_name( value )) && !wcsicmp( face->file, path ))
         {
+#ifndef SG_MUTANT_TRUST_EXTERNAL_RECORD
+            /* remembered, but the Fonts key no longer lists it: an uninstaller that shipped
+             * the same font took its entry away (LibreOffice's MSI, "Liberation Sans").
+             * Written again below; an entry an installer changed to its own file stays. */
+            if (winnt_key)
+            {
+                unsigned int name_size;
+                UNICODE_STRING nameW;
+                ULONG size;
+
+                if (tmp && !*tmp) *tmp = ' ';
+                name_size = lstrlenW( value ) * sizeof(WCHAR);
+                nameW.Buffer = value;
+                nameW.Length = nameW.MaximumLength = name_size;
+                if (NtQueryValueKey( winnt_key, &nameW, KeyValueBasicInformation, NULL, 0, &size )
+                    == STATUS_OBJECT_NAME_NOT_FOUND)
+                    continue;
+            }
+#endif
             face->flags |= ADDFONT_EXTERNAL_FOUND;
             continue;
         }
